 "AND_THE_HEADER_READING_IS_A_TRAP": "the parent carries BAYERPAT=RGGB, which reads as (0,0)=R (0,1)=G (1,0)=G (1,1)=B, and split_cfa emits in raster order \u2014 so the obvious inference is that channels 1 and 2 are the greens. THE DATA SAYS 0 AND 3. Corroborated three ways: those two share a median (1047 both) and a background MAD (10 ADU both) where the other pair reads 1037/9 and 1028/8, and their star counts match (992 vs 1007) where the others are 697 and 422. Whatever the row-order convention does, split_cfa's index order cannot be mapped to BAYERPAT by inspection \u2014 verify it against the pixels.",
